  "claim": "The band in the \"Art Wave\" scene, that had the first studio album You Could Have It So Much Better, is based in Glasgow.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Art Brut. Sentence: Named after French painter Jean Dubuffet's definition of outsider art - art by prisoners, loners, the mentally ill, and other marginalized people, and made without thought to imitation or presentation - South London's Art Brut were tagged by \"NME\" as part of the \"Art Wave\" scene that also included bands such as The Rakes, Franz Ferdinand and Bloc Party.\nPage: Franz Ferdinand (band). Sentence: Franz Ferdinand are a Scottish rock band, formed in 2002 and based in Glasgow.\nPage: You Could Have It So Much Better. Sentence: You Could Have It So Much Better is the second studio album by Scottish indie rock band Franz Ferdinand.",
