        "original_id": "c5881e7b-f0c3-5b4d-a811-7de2d706f708",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Art Brut, Franz Ferdinand, The Rakes, Bloc Party\n- People: Jean Dubuffet\n- Organizations: NME\n- Places: South London, Glasgow\n- Concepts: outsider art, Art Wave\n- Products: You Could Have It So Much Better\n\nFacts:\n- Jean Dubuffet defined outsider art as art by prisoners, loners, mentally ill people, and other marginalized people, made without thought to imitation or presentation.\n- Art Brut took their name from Jean Dubuffet's term \"Art Brut,\" which was tied to his definition of outsider art.\n- Franz Ferdinand is a Scottish rock band that formed in 2002 and is based in Glasgow.\n- NME tagged South London's Art Brut as part of the \"Art Wave\" scene.\n- The \"Art Wave\" scene included Art Brut, The Rakes, Franz Ferdinand, and Bloc Party.\n- You Could Have It So Much Better is the second studio album by Franz Ferdinand.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "47618c46-e855-5998-a5ab-7329a43fb073",
        "text": "Page: Art Brut. Sentence: Named after French painter Jean Dubuffet's definition of outsider art - art by prisoners, loners, the mentally ill, and other marginalized people, and made without thought to imitation or presentation - South London's Art Brut were tagged by \"NME\" as part of the \"Art Wave\" scene that also included bands such as The Rakes, Franz Ferdinand and Bloc Party.\nPage: Franz Ferdinand (band). Sentence: Franz Ferdinand are a Scottish rock band, formed in 2002 and based in Glasgow.\nPage: You Could Have It So Much Better. Sentence: You Could Have It So Much Better is the second studio album by Scottish indie rock band Franz Ferdinand.",
